# direnv: put this repo's flake devshell on PATH while working in the tree.
#
# Why: tools/kg-engine is Elixir, and scripts/task/kg-sidecar.sh resolves the
# interpreter from PATH first, then the store, then a substitution. With this
# file loaded, `elixir` is simply present — no nix call on any start, and the
# same store path the devshell pinned.
#
# Once per checkout:  direnv allow
use flake

# stdenv/setup exports SHELL as nixpkgs' non-interactive bash (no readline, no
# `complete` builtin, no `progcomp`), and direnv passes it on. Anything started
# from here that honours SHELL — kitty, tmux, editors — then launches a bash
# whose ~/.bashrc fails with "shopt: progcomp: invalid shell option name".
# The devShell puts bashInteractive first on PATH, so take the shell from PATH.
if command -v bash >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  export SHELL="$(command -v bash)"
fi
